;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-14, for Phase 17 (design section 20,
;; proposals 8 and 10, approved by the user); reviewed by the user,
;; 2026-10-14. Why this is right:
;; - forend.mod is llvm-for-loop-end's, built under -O2; on the guest it
;;   prints that fixture's expected (13 lines, count then the variable).
;; - Each FOR is as before at its head: the start assigned, then
;;   CMPx v, limit (TSTL for 0) and BLEQ counting up, BGEQ counting down
;;   (signed, these being signed variables), else JMP L^ out.
;; - After the body, the new end (proposal 8): SUBx3 at v's width gives
;;   the distance left, limit - v counting up (SUBW3 i, #32767), v - limit
;;   counting down (SUBW3 #-32768, i), CMPx R0 with the step's size (#1,
;;   #10, #2, #3, #4, #100), and BGEQU goes on to the step (INCx, DECx,
;;   ADDx2 #step, ADDx2 #-4); a smaller distance, unsigned, ends the loop
;;   (JMP L^), so v keeps the body's last value: 32767 (line 17), -32768
;;   (18), 120 (19, a SHORTINT: SUBB3, CMPB, ADDB2), 2147483646 (20), 10
;;   (23), 9 (24, BY 3), 2 (25), -3 (29, BY 100, the distance 6 being
;;   below 100); the HUGEINT ones MAX(HUGEINT) and MIN(HUGEINT).
;; - The HUGEINT loops (lines 21 and 22) take the distance as a quadword
;;   in R0/R1, SUBL2 then SBWC, and compare it unsigned with the step as
;;   QuadRelation does for a CARD64: CMPL R1, #0 with BLSSU/BGTRU, then
;;   CMPL R0, #step with BGEQU; R2 holds the result, BLBC R2 goes on to
;;   the step (ADDL2/ADWC), else JMP L^ out. Counting down from
;;   MIN(HUGEINT) the distance is v - MIN, SUBL2 #0, SBWC #^X80000000.
;; - Loops that do not run (lines 26 and 27, 5 TO 4 and 4 TO 5 BY -1)
;;   fail the head's test, so v stays the start. Line 28's body sets l to
;;   20; the distance, 10 - 20, is a large unsigned number, so the step is
;;   taken (21) and the head's signed test ends the loop, as the report's
;;   does.
;; - Report widens each value to a HUGEINT (CVTWL, CVTBL or MOVL, then
;;   ASHL #-31 for the high longword; MOVQ for h) and calls Out.Int, Char
;;   and Ln with G^, as Out's other users do; Out's key is the new one
;;   (Card and CardHex).
; forend, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
